    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0503" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 365.117/459</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Page to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-11-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 17, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>733. Department’s 324, April 18. Military authorities hold that, while Orocchi
                    may have lost Italian citizenship during minority <pb facs="0504" n="428"
                        xml:id="pg428"/> owing to naturalization his father, nevertheless, this fact
                    does not exempt him from military obligations towards Kingdom according terms
                    Article 12, Civil Code, held to be applicable in his case.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
